item.text:
I searched Portuguese and English queries across the STF, TSE, CGU, PRF, PF, MPF, TCU, major Brazilian reporting, and Reuters syndication. The strongest recoveries are: the PF’s favorable final conclusion in the general police-interference inquiry; a precise CGU ruling exposing and reversing the PRF’s unsupported secrecy position; Bolsonaro’s reported personal request that MEC prioritize a pastor’s network; the audited structure and limits of his asset and campaign disclosures; and later final judicial outcomes concerning PRF election interference.

Material gaps remain. I found no well-supported instance of voluntary costly candor or correction by Bolsonaro in 2022, and no affirmative integrity promise honored beyond legally required disclosure and belated personnel action. The public asset declaration is self-reported rather than an audit of origins. I found no final merits disposition specifically resolving Bolsonaro’s alleged MEC warning, while the jewelry matter remained unresolved at the stated cutoff. The accessible records establish Bolsonaro’s benefit from PRF activity and his wider leadership of the post-election project, but do not cleanly establish that he personally designed or ordered the October 30 road operations. Search results for his 2022 campaign-account case exposed the audit methodology and filed financial extract, but not a reliably accessible final judgment.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"PGR deve se manifestar sobre relatório que descarta interferência de Bolsonaro na PF","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://portal.stf.jus.br/noticias/verNoticiaDetalhe.asp?idConteudo=486020&ori=1","claim":"The Federal Police final report in INQ 4831 concluded that the investigation did not substantiate the alleged political interference by Bolsonaro in the Federal Police. The STF sent that report to the PGR for its prosecutorial position. This is strong contrary evidence, but the page records a police conclusion and referral rather than a final merits judgment by the Court.","locator":"Official STF summary, paragraphs headed “PGR deve se manifestar sobre relatório que descarta interferência de Bolsonaro na PF”; INQ 4831; final PF report transmitted April 27, 2022","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-001","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-pf-interference-inq4831-final-police-report","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.7"],"source_type":"official_court_procedural_record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official STF account of the investigation’s final police report and procedural status; it precisely distinguishes the PF conclusion from subsequent prosecutorial or judicial action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The final police report was completed and transmitted during 2022 and addresses alleged conduct during Bolsonaro’s presidency.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: INQ 4831 investigated Bolsonaro’s alleged interference, and the reported PF conclusion was favorable to him.","contrary_evidence":"Affirmative contrary evidence to claims that the general PF-interference allegation was proven; it does not dispose of the distinct June 2022 MEC-warning allegation.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-pf-interference-inq4831","lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Parecer nº 45/2023/CGRAI/OGU/CGU, processo 08198.032404/2022-28","publisher":"Controladoria-Geral da União","publication_date":"2023-03-03","url":"https://www.gov.br/cgu/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/2023/03/cgu-conclui-revisao-de-mais-oito-recursos-sobre-sigilos-a-informacoes-publicas/parecer-8.pdf","claim":"The PRF denied access to all planning records for its October 30, 2022 election operations using generalized security and unreasonableness arguments, supplied no specific justification or classification record when questioned, and maintained that position through internal appeals. The CGU found no basis for absolute secrecy and ordered disclosure within ten days, permitting only specifically justified redactions protecting officers.","locator":"Parecer 45/2023, pp. 1–3, paragraphs 1–8; pp. 5–6, concluding recommendation and Decision, especially PDF lines 247–284; process 08198.032404/2022-28","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-002","canonical_fact_key":"prf-2022-election-operation-records-unsupported-secrecy","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.7"],"source_type":"official_access_to_information_appellate_decision","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary CGU decision with exact administrative-process number, the PRF’s successive responses, legal analysis, and operative disclosure order.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The withholding occurred in response to a request filed over the PRF’s October 30, 2022 operation; the 2023 ruling specifically establishes that 2022 conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional rather than personal: the PRF was within Bolsonaro’s executive branch, but the decision does not show that Bolsonaro directed the withholding or the operation.","contrary_evidence":"The CGU allowed narrow redactions where disclosure could concretely endanger officers, so it did not hold that every withheld detail had to be public.","underlying_fact_key":"prf-2022-election-operation-records","lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Ministry of Education Prioritizes Pastors at Bolsonaro's Request","publisher":"Folha de S.Paulo","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/internacional/en/brazil/2022/03/ministry-of-education-prioritizes-pastors-at-bolsonaros-request.shtml","claim":"In a recorded MEC meeting, Education Minister Milton Ribeiro said that one priority was serving municipalities associated with Pastor Gilmar Santos and that this followed a special request from President Bolsonaro. The recording supplies direct evidence of Bolsonaro’s asserted personal direction of preferential access, although it is Ribeiro’s recorded account and not a judicial finding that Bolsonaro ordered corrupt payments or particular grants.","locator":"Article section reproducing and describing Ribeiro’s recorded MEC meeting statement; paragraphs beginning “These pastors have been intermediating access” and stating that Ribeiro said the arrangement responded to a request from Bolsonaro","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-003","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-requested-mec-priority-pastor-gilmar-network","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9"],"source_type":"investigative_reporting_with_primary_audio","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong independent reporting grounded in an underlying audio recording; the statement is direct as to Ribeiro’s account but does not itself adjudicate Bolsonaro’s intent or the legality of resulting allocations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The recording and disclosure concern MEC allocation practices active through March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct but attributed: Ribeiro expressly identified Bolsonaro as the source of the special request.","contrary_evidence":"Ribeiro later maintained that receiving the pastors did not mean they received improper treatment, and no accessible final judgment established Bolsonaro’s criminal responsibility for the arrangement.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-mec-pastor-priority-2022","lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Bolsonaro nomeia secretário-executivo Victor Veiga como ministro da Educação interino","publisher":"Reuters, syndicated by UOL","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/03/30/bolsonaro-nomeia-secretario-executivo-victor-veiga-como-ministro-da-educacao-interino.htm","claim":"After Milton Ribeiro requested dismissal amid the MEC influence allegations, Bolsonaro appointed the ministry’s executive secretary Victor Godoy Veiga as interim education minister. This is limited evidence of a personnel response to scrutiny, not proof that Bolsonaro initiated an integrity investigation, accepted responsibility, or selected an independent reformer.","locator":"Opening paragraph, dated March 30, 2022, identifying Ribeiro’s departure amid allegations and Bolsonaro’s appointment of the serving executive secretary as interim minister","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-004","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-replaced-ribeiro-with-victor-godoy-after-mec-scandal","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.8"],"source_type":"wire_service_reporting","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous reporting reliably establishes the appointment and immediate context, but the remedial significance requires cautious inference.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The appointment occurred on March 30, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: Bolsonaro made the interim ministerial appointment.","contrary_evidence":"Ribeiro requested dismissal, and replacing him with his own executive secretary is weaker evidence of affirmative integrity enforcement than an independently initiated removal or outside appointment.","underlying_fact_key":"mec-leadership-change-march-2022","lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Eleições 2022: consulte o patrimônio dos candidatos no portal do TSE","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Agosto/eleicoes-2022-consulte-o-patrimonio-dos-candidatos-no-portal-do-tse","claim":"Bolsonaro, like every 2022 candidate, filed a public declaration of assets through DivulgaCandContas. This supplies an official disclosure record but not an audit of beneficial ownership, acquisition history, source of funds, spouses’ or relatives’ property, or compatibility with income.","locator":"Official TSE page, sections explaining that the asset declaration is mandatory and publicly accessible through DivulgaCandContas","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-005","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-tse-public-asset-declaration","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.4","7B.8"],"source_type":"official_electoral_disclosure_system_description","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary TSE description of the legally required disclosure mechanism; its evidentiary limits are explicit because it is a candidate declaration rather than a forensic audit.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The disclosure was required and published for Bolsonaro’s 2022 reelection candidacy.","ruler_attribution":"Direct as to Bolsonaro’s filed declaration, but compliance was mandatory rather than voluntary.","contrary_evidence":"The record does not validate asset origins or exclude property held through relatives or third parties, so it cannot resolve the cash-property questions raised by WD012.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-asset-disclosure","lenses":["7B.4","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Extrato da prestação de contas final retificadora — Bolsonaro/Braga Netto 2022","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2023-02-06","url":"https://consultaunificadapje.tse.jus.br/consulta-publica-unificada/documento?extensaoArquivo=application%2Fpdf&path=tse%2F2023%2F2%2F6%2F13%2F2%2F20%2F796543dcfb8581745a5f3743a24c1cbff0154347cb74604b5a2d9c02039203c4","claim":"The Bolsonaro–Braga Netto campaign’s final amended account extract reported total receipts of R$123,459,663.00, including R$88,120,045.15 in financial donations from individuals, R$34,442,752.26 in party transfers, and R$536,139.81 in crowdfunding. The extract is an official filed dataset, not a finding that every receipt or expense was lawful or fully verified.","locator":"Final amended account extract, Revenue table §§1.1–1.9 and TOTAL DA RECEITA; associated proceeding PCE 0601079-87.2022.6.00.0000","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-006","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-braga-netto-2022-campaign-account-receipts","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.4","7B.9"],"source_type":"official_campaign_finance_filing","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary TSE-filed financial extract with exact account categories and totals; it is authoritative for reported figures but not for unqualified legal regularity.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The figures concern the Bolsonaro–Braga Netto 2022 presidential campaign, although the amended extract was filed in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Bolsonaro’s presidential ticket and campaign accounting, not necessarily to Bolsonaro’s personal knowledge of each transaction.","contrary_evidence":"No accessible final merits judgment was recovered, and the related sampling order confirms that examination was risk- and sample-based rather than a transaction-by-transaction forensic audit.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-campaign-finance-accounts","lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Prestação de Contas Eleitorais 0601079-87.2022.6.00.0000 — sampling order","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022-11-22","url":"https://www.jusbrasil.com.br/jurisprudencia/tse/1890573245","claim":"In Bolsonaro and Braga Netto’s 2022 campaign-account proceeding, the TSE authorized the electoral-accounts unit’s proposed sampling criteria because of the volume of financial resources and accounting entries and the limited statutory review period. This materially qualifies downstream descriptions of the campaign accounts as 'audited': the examination used an approved sampling plan.","locator":"PCE 0601079-87.2022.6.00.0000, introductory paragraphs and operative authorization adopting Informação Asepa nº 214/2022 under article 70 of Resolution-TSE 23.607/2019","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-007","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-campaign-account-sampling-method","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.4"],"source_type":"republication_of_official_electoral_order","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"The text reproduces an identifiable TSE order and exact case number, but the directly accessible copy is a secondary legal repository rather than the TSE docket itself.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The sampling decision concerns examination of Bolsonaro’s 2022 campaign accounts.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to the ticket’s accounts; it describes the tribunal’s audit method, not Bolsonaro’s personal conduct.","contrary_evidence":"Sampling does not imply that the filed accounts were unreliable; it means only that the audit cannot be characterized as exhaustive without the final technical report and judgment.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-2022-campaign-finance-accounts","lenses":["7B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"STF retira sigilo do caso das joias, dá acesso às partes e abre vista para análise da PGR","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2024-07-08","url":"https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/stf-retira-sigilo-do-caso-das-joias-da-acesso-as-partes-e-abre-vista-para-analise-da-pgr/","claim":"The Federal Police completed and submitted its final report in the Saudi-jewelry investigation, after which the STF removed secrecy and gave the PGR fifteen days to seek further evidence, request archiving, or bring charges. The official notice confirms completion of the police phase but explicitly shows that no prosecutorial or judicial merits disposition then existed.","locator":"Opening three paragraphs; PET 11645; order dated July 8, 2024; passage listing the PGR’s three procedural options","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-008","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-saudi-jewelry-final-pf-report-procedural-status","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.4","7B.6"],"source_type":"official_court_procedural_record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official STF notice precisely identifying the completed investigative phase and remaining prosecutorial options.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The later procedural record specifically concerns Bolsonaro’s handling of official gifts connected to his presidency, including conduct extending into 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: Bolsonaro was a subject of PET 11645 and the investigated handling and attempted recovery of the gifts.","contrary_evidence":"Completion of a PF report is not a conviction or final finding; the later WD011 update likewise remained procedurally unresolved.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-saudi-jewelry-investigation","lenses":["7B.4","7B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"STF arquiva inquérito contra dois delegados da PF acusados de tentar barrar eleitores em 2022","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2026-01-16","url":"https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/stf-arquiva-inquerito-contra-dois-delegados-da-pf-acusados-de-tentar-barrar-eleitores-em-2022/","claim":"The STF archived the separate investigation of two Federal Police delegates on double-jeopardy grounds because the road-blocking conduct had already been adjudicated in APs 2668 and 2663. The official summary states that Anderson Torres, Silvinei Vasques, and Marília Ferreira Alencar were convicted for crimes connected to the 2022 election obstruction, while Fernando de Sousa Oliveira was acquitted. This supplies final dispositions for senior officials, but not by itself proof that Bolsonaro personally ordered the PRF operation.","locator":"Official summary, paragraph explaining the non bis in idem basis and identifying the convictions and acquittal in APs 2668 and 2663","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-009","canonical_fact_key":"prf-pf-2022-election-obstruction-final-criminal-dispositions","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.7"],"source_type":"official_court_disposition_summary","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official STF account of final adjudicative outcomes, with exact related criminal-action numbers and a clear distinction between convicted and acquitted officials.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The later decisions adjudicate conduct during the October 2022 presidential election.","ruler_attribution":"Shared-authority and beneficiary nexus only in this record: the convicted officials served Bolsonaro’s administration and the interference favored his reelection, but this particular summary does not establish his personal instruction.","contrary_evidence":"One official was acquitted, and the source does not attribute the operational order directly to Bolsonaro.","underlying_fact_key":"prf-2022-election-obstruction","lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Barroso acolhe pedido da PGR e manda arquivar pedidos de investigação contra Bolsonaro","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/barroso-acolhe-pedido-da-pgr-e-manda-arquivar-pedidos-de-investigacao-contra-bolsonaro/","claim":"The STF archived PETs 10436 and 10439, which sought an investigation of Bolsonaro for possible prevarication, passive corruption, or embezzlement involving Petrobras. The two witnesses whose messages triggered the petitions denied knowing of criminal conduct, and the PGR found no just cause to open a criminal investigation.","locator":"Official summary, first four paragraphs; PET 10436 and PET 10439; decision dated November 29, 2022","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-C1-010","canonical_fact_key":"bolsonaro-petrobras-petitions-10436-10439-archived","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6"],"source_type":"official_court_disposition_summary","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official STF disposition identifying the allegations, witness denials, PGR position, and legal basis for archiving.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The petitions and final archival decision occurred in 2022 during Bolsonaro’s presidency.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the requested investigation concerned Bolsonaro personally.","contrary_evidence":"Strong favorable disposition for these specific Petrobras allegations; it does not resolve unrelated fuel-pricing policy concerns or other scrutiny matters.","underlying_fact_key":"bolsonaro-petrobras-criminal-allegations-2022","lenses":["7B.6"]}
